FILE: app/src/globe-tilt.ts
```ts
import type { GeospatialCamera } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function tiltGlobeCamera(camera: GeospatialCamera, pitch: number): void {
  const limits = camera.limits;

  limits.pitchDisabledRadiusScale = null;
  limits.pitchMax = Math.max(limits.pitchMax, pitch);
  limits.pitchMin = Math.min(limits.pitchMin, pitch);

  camera._setOrientation(camera.yaw, pitch, camera.radius, camera.center);
  camera.pitch = pitch;
}
```

I made the pitch limits radius-independent and wide enough, then reapplied the orientation with the current yaw/radius/center so only the tilt changes. I wasn't sure whether `_setOrientation` always assigns `pitch`, so I set it explicitly, and I assumed nulling `pitchDisabledRadiusScale` disables radius-dependent pitch clamping.
